// The Chinese lunisolar calendar, and the Korean (Dangi) one that differs
// from it only in being reckoned at Seoul's meridian rather than China's.
//
// A month begins on the day of a new moon; a year has twelve months, or
// thirteen when one month contains no major solar term and is repeated as
// a leap month. Both depend on astronomy, so the months of 1900 to 2100
// are ICU's, computed by its astronomer and tabulated here; the year is
// the Gregorian year in which the Chinese year begins (ICU's "related
// year"). Dates outside the table give `None`.

type ChineseDate = {
    related_year: i64,
    month: i64,
    leap: bool,
    day: i64,
}

type LunisolarKind =
    | China
    | Korea

